ystemPatterns.md`: AI reads → rule engine decides → AI explains; all AI calls go through `src/server/ai.ts` (zod check, one retry, safe fallback); only the store module writes to the database; folder layout; Aadhaar masking; no images stored.\n- `techContext.md`: the stack from `03-stack.md`, the versions above, the npm scripts, and the `.env.local` keys.\n- `activeContext.md`: the current task (T0), decisions made, and next step (T1).\n- `progress.md`: what's done, what's left (T1–T4, T-last) and known issues.\n\n**Scaffold (from create-next-app, then adjusted)**\n- `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `tsconfig.json` (`\"strict\": true`), `next.config.ts`, `postcss.config.mjs`, `eslint.config.mjs`, `next-env.d.ts`, `public\\*`\n- `src\\app\\layout.tsx`: `lang=\"hi\"` and the page title in metadata.\n- `src\\app\\page.tsx`: the placeholder page, titled \"KaagazCheck: कागज़ चेक\" with a one-line pitch.\n- `src\\app\\globals.css`: Tailwind v4 (`@import \"tailwindcss\"`).\n\n**New files**\n- `src\\core\\appInfo.ts`: plain constants (`APP_TITLE`, `APP_TAGLINE_EN/HI`) with no UI imports. The page reads its title from here.\n- `src\\core\\appInfo.test.ts`: the smoke test. It checks that `APP_TITLE` is exactly \"KaagazCheck: कागज़ चेक\", which also catches broken Hindi text. Because it doesn't render React, there's no need for jsdom or testing-library.\n- `vitest.config.ts`: Node environment, picks up `src/**/*.test.ts`, and handles the `@/` alias.\n- `.env.example`: just `CLINE_API_KEY=` and `CLINE_MODEL=`.\n- `.gitignore` (create-next-app writes one; I'll edit it): ignore `node_modules/`, `.next/`, `out/`, `*.db` (plus `-wal`/`-shm`), `.env.local` and `.env*.local`, `*.tsbuildinfo`. I'll remove its default `.env*` line so `.env.example` still gets committed, and I won't ignore `.cline-runs/`.\n- `README.md`: a short placeholder (name, pitch, setup). The full README comes in T-last.\n- `tasks\\LOG.md`: I'll add a T0 entry (files changed, pass/fail counts, open issues, requests for Claude).\n\nI won't touch `tasks/NEXT.md`, `tasks/backlog/`, `docs/`, `.clinerules/` or `.cline-runs/`. `src/server/ai.ts` and the database store are left for T1–T3.\n\n## Commands (PowerShell, run from `C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build`)\n```powershell\ngit init -b main\nnpx create-next-app@16.4.0 \"$env:TEMP\\kc-scaffold\" --ts --tailwind --eslint --app --src-dir --import-alias \"@/*\" --use-npm --no-turbopack --yes --skip-install\n# copy everything except node_modules/.git into this folder; nothing existing gets overwritten\nrobocopy \"$env:TEMP\\kc-scaffold\" . /E /XD node_modules .git /XC /XN /XO\nnpm install\nnpm install zod\nnpm install -D vitest fast-check\nnpm test            # vitest run\nnpm run typecheck   # tsc --noEmit\nnpm run lint        # eslint .\nnpm run build       # next build\ngit add -A\ngit commit -m \"T0: scaffold + memory bank\"\n```\n\nnpm scripts:\n\n| Script | Command |\n|---|---|\n| `dev` | `next dev` |\n| `build` | `next build` |\n| `start` | `next start` |\n| `lint` | `eslint .` |\n| `typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` |\n| `test` | `vitest run` |\n| `test:watch` | `vitest` |\n\nIf a flag in the create-next-app command doesn't work, I'll drop it. If the temp-folder approach fails, I'll write the same scaffold files by hand.\n\n## Risks and how I'll handle them\n1. **create-next-app refuses a folder with other files in it.** Generating in a temp folder and copying with `robocopy` avoids that, and the copy options never overwrite existing files. One catch: `robocopy` returns exit code 1 when it succeeds, so that isn't an error.\n2. **The default `.gitignore` hides `.env.example`.** create-next-app adds `.env*`, which matches `.env.example` too, so I'll replace that line. Before committing, `git status` should show `.env.example` and `.cline-runs/` but not `.env.local`.\n3. **Next 16 removed `next lint`.** So the lint script runs `eslint .` with the generated config, and I'll set it to skip `.next/`, `.cline-runs/` and `docs/`.\n4. **Hindi text could get garbled on Windows.** Windows PowerShell 5.1 doesn't save files as UTF-8 by default. I'll write every file with the editor tool, never `Set-Content` or `>`, and the smoke test checks the Devanagari title.\n5. **The folder path has a space** (\"cline hackathon\"). All paths will be quoted, and the package name will be `kaagazcheck`.\n6. **Vitest 5 is a new major version.** If it clashes with the Vite version Next uses or with Node 24, I'll pin the latest working version and note it in `techContext.md`.\n7. **Smaller build issues.** A Turbopack build problem on Windows could be fixed with `next build --webpack`. The Tailwind v4 setup (`@tailwindcss/postcss`) comes from the scaffold, so there's nothing to set up by hand.\n8. **Scope.** No AI calls, database or real features in T0, and no personal data. The page has no inputs.\n\n## How we'll know it's done\n- `npm test` passes (1 file, at least 1 test).\n- `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint` and `npm run build` all pass.\n- The 5"}}
